  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scaling-up and Sustaining Anti-Malaria Interventions in Ethiopia - Ethiopia (01-Jul-2015-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ethiopia, Malaria, Federal Ministry of Health of the Federal Democratic Republic of Ethiopia (FMOH)This program has the following goals: By 2020, to achieve near zero malaria deaths (no more than one confirmed malaria death per 100,000 population at risk) in Ethiopia..  By 2020, to eliminate malaria in selected low transmission areas..  By 2020, to reduce malaria cases by 75% from baseline of 2013.. The objectives of this program are: By 2015 and beyond, 100% of confirmed malaria cases are treated according to the national guidelines.  By 2015 and beyond, ensure and maintain universal access of the population at risk to at least one type of globally recommended anti-vector intervention.  By 2017 and beyond, 100% of suspected malaria cases are diagnosed using RDTs or microscopy within 24 hours of fever onset.  By 2020, 100% complete data and evidence will be generated at all levels within designated time periods to facilitate appropriate decision making.  By 2020, achieve and sustain zero indigenous transmission of malaria in 50 selected districts.  By 2020, all households living in malaria endemic areas will have the knowledge, attitudes and practice towards malaria prevention and control</narrative>
  </description>
